Notes and operational considerations:
- I implemented cache helpers that try to support multiple cache client signatures (Redis-like set(nx/ex), memcache add, simple set with ttl), and decode bytes returned from cache.get. If this project has a canonical cache wrapper API with documented method names (e.g., set(key, value, ex=.., nx=..)), I can simplify the helpers to use the canonical calls.
- The implementation now raises an explicit PaymentError if we successfully processed the payment at the gateway but were unable to persist idempotency state after multiple retries; this is deliberate to avoid silent duplicate-charge windows — we can change this policy if you'd prefer returning success to the caller and raising an operator alert instead.
- I avoided logging raw response bodies to reduce risk of sensitive data leakage and log only status and gateway request id header when available.

